['To solve this problem, you can use a library like Jansson which is a C library for parsing, manipulating, iterating and creating JSON data. Below is an example of how to write the function in C using jansson. 

Please note that in real world applications, it's more practical to use HTTP libraries like libcurl or higher-level API wrapper libraries which handle these details for you. This implementation does not take into account network latency, error handling etc. Also, this code doesn't check the `access_token` on server side as OAuth2 access tokens are opaque and can only be validated by making a request to authorization server with it.

```c
#include <jansson.h>
#include <string.h>

bool validateAccessToken(const char* jsonString) {
    json_error_t error;
    json_t *root = json_loads(jsonString, 0, &error);

    if(!root) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Error parsing JSON: on line %d: %s\n", error.line, error.text);
        return false;
    }

    json_t *accessToken = json_object_get(root, "access_token");
    if(!json_is_string(accessToken) || !strlen(json_string_value(accessToken))) {
        json_decref(root);
        return false;
    }

    json_t *expiresIn = json_object_get(root, "expires_in");
    if(!json_is_integer(expiresIn) || json_integer_value(expiresIn) > 604800 || json_integer_value(expiresIn) < 0 ) {
        json_decref(root);
        return false;
    }

    json_t *tokenType = json_object_get(root, "token_type");
    if(!json_is_string(tokenType) || strcmp(json_string_value(tokenType),"Bearer")) {
        json_decref(root);
        return false;
    }

    json_t *refreshToken = json_object_get(root, "refresh_token");
    if(refreshToken && (!json_is_string(refreshToken) || !strlen(json_string_value(refreshToken)))){
        json_decref(root);
        return false;
    }

    json_decref(root);
    return true;
}
```
To compile and link the code you need to install jansson development package and link against it. 
For example, in Ubuntu you can do:
```bash
sudo apt-get install libjansson-dev
gcc -o validateAccessToken validateAccessToken.c -ljansson
```
']

