            try {
                if (!Files.exists(filePath)) {
                    System.err.println("File does not exist: " + filePath);
                    return null;
                }

                // Assume compressed state file is gzip for this example
                InputStream in = new GZIPInputStream(new FileInputStream(filePath.toFile()));

                try (ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(in)) {
                    MoSTState loadedState = (MoSTState) ois.readObject();

                    // Check integrity of the state object with checksum provided by caller
                    MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
                    if (!checksum.equals(bytesToHex(md.digest(serialize(loadedState))))) {
                        System.err.println("Checksum mismatch for file: " + filePath);
                        return null;
                    }

                    stateRef.set(loadedState);
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    System.err.println("Failed to load state from file: " + filePath + ". Attempt: " + retryCount + 1 + ", Cause: " + e);
                    // Sleep before retrying, you can use exponential backoff strategy here if needed
                    Thread.sleep(100 * (retryCount + 1)); 
                }
            } catch (Exception e) {
                System.err.println("Failed to load state from file: " + filePath + ". Attempt: " + retryCount + 1 + ", Cause: " + e);
                // Sleep before retrying, you can use exponential backoff strategy here if needed
                Thread.sleep(100 * (retryCount + 1)); 
            }
        }

        return stateRef.get();
    }

    private byte[] serialize(Object obj) throws IOException {
        ByteArrayOutputStream baos = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
        ObjectOutputStream oos = new ObjectOutputStream(baos);
        oos.writeObject(obj);
        return baos.toByteArray();
    }

    private String bytesToHex(byte[] bytes) {
        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
        for (byte b : bytes) {
            result.append(String.format("%02x", b));
        }
        return result.toString();
    }
}
``` 

This class is designed to load a state object from file, handle exceptions gracefully and retry up to three times in case of transient errors like file access failures. It decompresses the file using GZIPInputStream on-the-fly during loading without storing the decompressed content in memory. After deserialization, it checks the integrity of the loaded state object with a checksum provided by caller. If the checksums do not match, it logs an error and returns null. This class is thread safe as it uses AtomicReference for maintaining atomicity when setting the loaded state object reference.

Please note that distributed system considerations are out of scope here. For such requirements, you would need to integrate with a service discovery mechanism, use consensus algorithms (Paxos, Raft etc.) or some form of messaging queues/topics and possibly distributed databases like Apache Cassandra or Apache Zookeeper for storing state objects. Also remember that this will increase complexity and may affect performance.
']

