['Below is an example solution for this problem using the JSch library in Java:

```java
import com.jcraft.jsch.*;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
import java.util.concurrent.Executors;
import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public class SFTPTransferManager {
    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SFTPTransferManager.class);
    private static final int MAX_RETRIES = 3;
    private static final long BASE_DELAY = 5000L;
    private static final String SFTP_SERVER = "sftp.server.com";
    private static final String USERNAME = "username";
    private static final String PASSWORD = "password";
    private static final int PORT = 22;
    private JSch jsch = new JSch();
    private Session session;
    private ChannelSftp channelSftp;
    private ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10); // Set the number of threads as per your requirement
    private AtomicInteger fileCounter = new AtomicInteger(0);

    public SFTPTransferManager() throws JSchException {
        session = jsch.getSession(USERNAME, SFTP_SERVER, PORT);
        session.setPassword(PASSWORD);

        java.util.Properties config = new java.util.Properties();
        config.put("StrictHostKeyChecking", "no");
        session.setConfig(config);
        session.connect();

        channelSftp = (ChannelSftp) session.openChannel("sftp");
        channelSftp.connect();
    }

    public void transferFile(String localPath, String remotePath) {
        executor.submit(() -> doTransfer(localPath, remotePath));
    }

    private void doTransfer(String localPath, String remotePath) {
        int attempt = 0;
        while (attempt <= MAX_RETRIES) {
            try {
                channelSftp.put(new FileInputStream(localPath), remotePath);
                logger.info("File {} transfer was successful", fileCounter.incrementAndGet());
                return;
            } catch (JSchException | SftpException e) {
                if (attempt == MAX_RETRIES) {
                    logger.error("Failed to transfer file after {} attempts: {}", attempt, localPath);
                    return;
                } else {
                    long delay = BASE_DELAY * ((long) Math.pow(2, attempt)); // Exponential backoff
                    logger.warn("Transfer failed for file {}, retrying in {}ms (attempt {}/{})", localPath, delay, attempt + 1, MAX_RETRIES);
                    try {
                        Thread.sleep(delay);
                    } catch (InterruptedException e2) {
                        // Handle interruption if necessary
                    }
                }
            }
            attempt++;
        }
    }

    public void shutdown() throws JSchException {
        executor.shutdown();
        try {
            if (!executor.awaitTermination(5, TimeUnit.MINUTES)) {
                executor.shutdownNow();
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            executor.shutdownNow();
        }

        channelSftp.exit();
        session.disconnect();
    }
}
```
This code uses a thread pool to execute file transfers concurrently, with each transfer running in its own thread. The `transferFile` method is called to initiate a file transfer, which adds a task to the executor service that performs the transfer. 

The `doTransfer` method implements the retry logic using exponential backoff. If a transfer fails due to an exception, it waits for an increasing amount of time before retrying, up to three times. After all retries have been exhausted, the method logs an error and returns.

Finally, the `shutdown` method shuts down the executor service and disconnects from the SFTP server. It also handles gracefully interrupting threads that are still waiting for a transfer to complete after a timeout. 

Please note that you need to include JSch library (version 0.1.54 or higher) and Slf4j in your project for this code to work properly. Also, make sure to replace SFTP_SERVER, USERNAME, PASSWORD with actual server address, username and password respectively. 

This is a simplified example and may need adjustments based on your specific requirements. For instance, you might want to handle different types of exceptions more specifically or add additional logging for debugging purposes.
']

