typedef struct {
    int max_weighted_sum;
    char* transaction_id;
} Metrics;

Metrics metrics = {0, NULL};

int validateOAuthToken(const char *json) 
{
    json_error_t error;
    json_t *root = json_loads(json, 0, &error);

    if(!root) return 0; // Invalid JSON

    int result = 1;
    const char* fields[] = {"access_token", "expires_in", "token_type"};

    for (int i=0; i<3; ++i) {
        json_t *value = json_object_get(root, fields[i]);

        if(!json_is_string(value))  result = 0; // Field not a string
        else if (!strlen(json_string_value(value)))  result = 0; // String is empty

        if (i == 1 && (json_integer_value(value) > 604800 || json_integer_value(value) <= 0))  result = 0; // expires_in not in range
        else if (i == 2 && strcmp(json_string_value(value), "Bearer"))  result = 0; // token_type not Bearer

    }

    json_t *refresh_token = json_object_get(root, "refresh_token");
    if (refresh_token && (!json_is_string(refresh_token) || !strlen(json_string_value(refresh_token))))  result = 0; // refresh_token not a non-empty string

    json_decref(root);

    return result;
}

void filterTransactions(const char *transactions[]) {

    time_t now = time(NULL);
    int transactionsCount = 0;
    int weightedSum = 0;
    const char* maxWeightedTransactionId = NULL;

    for (int i=0; transactions[i] != NULL; ++i) {
        json_error_t error;
        json_t *root = json_loads(transactions[i], 0, &error);

        if(!root) continue; // Invalid JSON

        json_t* age = json_object_get(root, "age");
        time_t transactionTime = now - json_integer_value(age);
        json_t* pastTransactionsCount = json_object_get(root, "past3SecondsTransactionsCount");

        // Skip transactions older than 10 minutes or with more than 3 transactions in the last 3 seconds
        if (difftime(now, transactionTime) > 600 || json_integer_value(pastTransactionsCount) > 3) {
            json_decref(root);
            continue;
        }

        json_t* weight = json_object_get(root, "weight");
        weightedSum += json_integer_value(weight);
        ++transactionsCount;

        if (metrics.max_weighted_sum < weightedSum) { // Update metrics and max transaction id
            metrics.max_weighted_sum = weightedSum;
            json_t* transactionId = json_object_get(root, "id");
            metrics.transaction_id = strdup(json_string_value(transactionId));
        }

        json_decref(root);
    }

}
```

This code uses the jansson library for JSON processing. It includes a `validateOAuthToken` function that parses and validates an OAuth token based on the provided criteria. The `filterTransactions` function filters transactions based on age, number of past 3 second transactions, and weight, updating metrics as necessary.
']

['Here's an example implementation in C#:
```Csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.IO;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Microsoft.Azure.Storage; // Assumes Azure Storage as cloud service
using Microsoft.Azure.Storage.Blob;

public class FileMetadata
{
    public string FilePath { get; set; }
    public DateTime UploadTime { get; set; }
    public string CloudURL { get; set; }
}

public interface IFileUploadService
{
    Task<List<FileMetadata>> ProcessFilesAsync(IEnumerable<string> filePaths);
}

public class AzureBlobStorageService : IFileUploadService
{
    private readonly CloudBlobClient blobClient;
    private readonly string containerName = "mycontainer"; // Update with your actual container name

    public AzureBlobStorageService(string storageConnectionString)
    {
        var storageAccount = CloudStorageAccount.Parse(storageConnectionString);
        blobClient = storageAccount.CreateCloudBlobClient();
        blobClient.DefaultRequestOptions.RetryPolicy = new Microsoft.WindowsAzure.Storage.RetryPolicies.ExponentialRetry();
    }

    public async Task<List<FileMetadata>> ProcessFilesAsync(IEnumerable<string> filePaths)
    {
        var metadataList = new List<FileMetadata>();

        foreach (var path in filePaths)
        {
            try
            {
                using (var stream = File.OpenRead(path))
                {
                    var container = blobClient.GetContainerReference(containerName);
                    await container.CreateIfNotExistsAsync();
                    var blockBlob = container.GetBlockBlobReference(Path.GetFileName(path));
                    await blockBlob.UploadFromStreamAsync(stream);

                    metadataList.Add(new FileMetadata
                    {
                        FilePath = path,
                        UploadTime = DateTime.Now,
                        CloudURL = blockBlob.Uri.ToString()
                    });
                }
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                // Handle exceptions here e.g., log the error and continue to next file
                Console.WriteLine($"An error occurred while processing '{path}': {ex.Message}");
            }
        }

        return metadataList;
    }
}
```
This solution uses Azure Blob Storage as cloud service, but you can easily modify it to use any other storage service like AWS S3 or Google Cloud Storage by implementing the IFileUploadService interface with their respective SDK. The files are processed one at a time for simplicity and because network latency could be an issue when batching uploads. Error handling is rudimentary, but you can add more sophisticated error logging and recovery logic as needed. Note that this code assumes that there's already a valid connection string available for Azure Blob Storage; modify it to suit your needs.
']

["Here's the Java code block that includes the mentioned method:

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.time.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class LogEntry {
    LocalDateTime timestamp;
    Level logLevel;

    public enum Level { DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR }
}

class LogManager {
    private final Queue<LogEntry> queue = new ConcurrentLinkedQueue<>();
    private final Map<String, AtomicLong> rollingAverageMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final int RETENTION_PERIOD = 10; // for example

    public void processLogEntry(LogEntry entry) {
        Level thresholdLevel = LogLevel.INFO; // for example

        if (entry.logLevel.ordinal() >= thresholdLevel.ordinal()) {
            synchronized (rollingAverageMap) {
                AtomicLong rollingAverage = rollingAverageMap.get(entry.timestamp.toString());

                if (rollingAverage == null) {
                    rollingAverage = new AtomicLong();
                    rollingAverageMap.put(entry.timestamp.toString(), rollingAverage);
                }

                rollingAverage.set(queue.stream()
                        .filter(e -> e.logLevel.ordinal() >= thresholdLevel.ordinal())
                        .mapToLong(e -> Duration.between(entry.timestamp, e.timestamp).toMillis()).average().orElse(0));
            }

            queue.offer(entry);
        }

        if (queue.size() > RETENTION_PERIOD) {
            LogEntry expiredLog = queue.poll();
            rollingAverageMap.remove(expiredLog.timestamp.toString());
        }
    }
}
```

This code provides a `processLogEntry` method that can handle log entries in a multithreaded environment, maintaining an updated rolling average of the timestamps for logs above a specified threshold. The size of the window is determined by the retention period, which defines how many logs are kept and used to calculate the rolling average. The code ensures thread safety by synchronizing access to shared resources.
"]

