['Here is a Java method named `processLogEntries` that fulfills all your requirements. This method uses Java's built-in `hashCode()` function for converting each log entry into a unique identifier. It also ensures thread safety by using `ConcurrentHashMap` and `synchronized` keyword to avoid data corruption. For logging, we will use Java Logging API (JUL). Lastly, efficient memory usage is ensured through the use of streaming operations when processing large collections.

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.logging.Level;
import java.util.logging.Logger;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

public class LogProcessor {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(LogProcessor.class.getName());
    private ConcurrentHashMap<String, String> processedEntries = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public void processLogEntries(List<LogEntry> logEntries) {
        long startTime = System.nanoTime();

        Stream<LogEntry> streamOfEntries = logEntries.parallelStream().filter(Objects::nonNull);
        logger.log(Level.INFO, "Processing started at {0}", new Date());

        try {
            streamOfEntries.forEachOrdered(entry -> {
                String identifier = null;

                try {
                    identifier = Integer.toString(entry.hashCode());
                } catch (NullPointerException e) {
                    logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Malformed entry detected and ignored: {0}", e);
                }

                if (identifier != null) {
                    synchronized (processedEntries) {
                        processedEntries.putIfAbsent(identifier, entry.getMessage());
                    }
                }
            });
        } finally {
            long totalTime = System.nanoTime() - startTime;
            logger.log(Level.INFO, "Processing finished at {0}, took {1} nanoseconds", new Object[]{new Date(), totalTime});
        }
    }

    public static class LogEntry {
        private final String timestamp;
        private final String message;

        public LogEntry(String timestamp, String message) {
            this.timestamp = timestamp;
            this.message = message;
        }

        public String getMessage() {
            return message;
        }

        @Override
        public int hashCode() {
            // Custom implementation of hash function here, for instance using Apache Commons HashCodeBuilder
            return Objects.hash(timestamp, message);
        }
    }
}
```
This code creates a `ConcurrentHashMap` that maps identifiers to log messages. A `Stream` is created from the list of log entries to process them in parallel. Each entry gets converted into an identifier and put into the map if it's not already there. All processing time and status are logged using JUL logger, including start and end times.
']

['```java
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.List;
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class FileHasher {
    private ExecutorService executor = Executors.newCachedThreadPool();

    public Future<String> hashFile(Path path) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, IOException {
        return executor.submit(() -> {
            MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
            try (InputStream is = Files.newInputStream(path)) {
                byte[] buffer = new byte[8192];
                int len;
                while ((len = is.read(buffer)) != -1) {
                    md.update(buffer, 0, len);
                }
            }
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
            for (byte b : md.digest()) {
                sb.append(String.format("%02x", b));
            }
            return sb.toString();
        });
    }

    public void hashFiles(List<Path> paths) throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException, IOException {
        List<Future<String>> futures = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();

        for (Path path : paths) {
            futures.add(hashFile(path));
        }

        for (Future<String> future : futures) {
            System.out.println("Hash: " + future.get());
        }
    }
}
```
