['Here is a sample implementation of your requirement in Java using concurrent programming and Java's built-in features like `Executors`, `Callable` and `Future`. This implementation uses `SHA-256` hashing algorithm and simple logging mechanism using `java.util.logging` package:

```java
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;

public class FileHasher {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(FileHasher.class.getName());
    private ExecutorService executor;

    public FileHasher(int threads) {
        this.executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(threads);
    }

    public Map<String, String> hashFilesInParallel(List<String> filePaths) throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException {
        List<Callable<Map<String, byte[]>>> tasks = new ArrayList<>();
        for (String path : filePaths) {
            Callable<Map<String, byte[]>> task = () -> Collections.singletonMap(path, readFile(path));
            tasks.add(task);
        }

        Map<String, String> results = new HashMap<>();
        List<Future<Map<String, byte[]>>> futures = executor.invokeAll(tasks);

        for (Future<Map<String, byte[]>> future : futures) {
            Map<String, byte[]> fileContents = future.get(); // This blocks until the task is done or throws an exception if it was interrupted
            for (Map.Entry<String, byte[]> entry : fileContents.entrySet()) {
                results.put(entry.getKey(), hashWithSha256(entry.getValue()));
            }
        }

        return results;
    }

    private String hashWithSha256(byte[] data) {
        try {
            MessageDigest digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
            byte[] hashBytes = digest.digest(data);

            StringBuilder hexString = new StringBuilder();
            for (byte b : hashBytes) {
                String hex = Integer.toHexString(0xFF & b);
                if (hex.length() == 1) {
                    hexString.append('0');
                }
                hexString.append(hex);
            }

            return hexString.toString();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to hash data with SHA-256", e);
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to hash data with SHA-256", e);
        }
    }

    private byte[] readFile(String path) {
        try {
            return Files.readAllBytes(Paths.get(path));
        } catch (Exception e) {
            logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to read file at: " + path, e);
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to read file at: " + path, e);
        }
    }

    public void shutdown() {
        executor.shutdown();
    }
}
```
This class uses a thread pool where each task is to read the contents of a file and compute its hash. It leverages Java's concurrency API to start all tasks asynchronously, then waits for them all to finish before returning results. If any task fails, it throws an `ExecutionException` from the main method, which can be caught at a higher level to handle errors gracefully.

Please note that this is a simplified implementation and does not include features like configurable batch sizes or support for other hash algorithms. You could enhance this class by adding those features in your actual usage scenario.
']

